      "writtenOn": "2023-11-08T23:06:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "not for this CL, but you know what might be interesting?\n\nRather than let `patch.backup` be null outside of patch/restore, we can put it to use. When we are setting up the patch-array clones, we can precalculate the pointer for `patch.bytesPerPixel * (dy * ctx-\u003estride + dx)` at the first scanline\u0027s tail and store that in `patch.backup`.\n\nThen on each scanline, we can just swap in `patch.backup` in patch, and on restore we can swap it back and add `ctx-\u003estride`.\n\nThis isn\u0027t a huge improvement but it\u0027s per-patch _and_ per-scanline so a 1000-scanline draw with two patches could save 4000 multiplies.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1147,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1149,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "3f0ad62168b8af56301f7f1b1201cf3356a20f16",
